{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784301801,"nonce":"ofZC/VuiRPUdQ5nJ1xnW81gcX64=","title":"[dogfood] artifacts harvested + uploaded but never indexed (API returns []) — annotation/scheduler race","message":"A succeeded step's artifacts land in the object store AND on the Pod's scarab.io/artifacts annotation, but GET /v1/runs/{id}/artifacts returns []. The durable index the API reads (db.artifacts_of_run) is never populated.\n\nCause (scheduler.rs ~867): on ExecState::Succeeded the scheduler calls executor.artifacts(handle) — which reads the Pod's scarab.io/artifacts annotation — and only db.put_artifacts(...) if non-empty. But the k8s executor writes that annotation from harvest_artifacts() in the settle path, which execs `tar` in the egress sidecar and patches the annotation AFTER the step container has already exited (i.e. after poll() can observe Succeeded). So the scheduler can read the annotation before harvest has written it -\u003e empty -\u003e put_artifacts skipped -\u003e API empty forever, even though the blobs and annotation both exist.\n\nEvidence (dogfood run 68af6899, colima):\n- .scarab/objects/artifacts/68af6899.../{toolchain.txt,checked-sha.txt} present on disk.\n- Pod annotation scarab.io/artifacts lists both with object_key.\n- GET /v1/runs/68af6899.../artifacts =\u003e [].\n\nFix direction: make artifact indexing observe the harvest completion (e.g. harvest+annotate before the step is reported Succeeded to the scheduler, or have the scheduler re-read after the egress/settle barrier, or persist the index from the executor at harvest time rather than relying on a later annotation read).","files":null}]}